---
const problems = [
  {
    icon: '⚡',
    title: 'Stuck on End-of-Life PHP Versions',
    description:
      'Running PHP 5.6 or 7.x exposes your business to severe unpatched security vulnerabilities, compliance failures (SOC2/PCI), and compatibility blockers with modern libraries.',
  },
  {
    icon: '🕸️',
    title: 'The Fragile "House of Cards"',
    description:
      'Spaghetti code, global state, and massive God classes make every minor bugfix or feature release terrifying. Your team hesitates to touch critical revenue-generating flows.',
  },
  {
    icon: '💣',
    title: 'The Risky "Full Rewrite" Trap',
    description:
      'Agencies love recommending multi-year, million-dollar rewrites in new languages. Most of these blow past deadlines, exceed budgets, and fail to replicate legacy edge cases.',
  },
  {
    icon: '🐢',
    title: 'Degrading Latency & Spiraling Server Costs',
    description:
      'Unindexed SQL queries, N+1 query loops, and memory bloat choke your database during peak hours, forcing you to overprovision cloud infrastructure to survive.',
  },
];
---

<section id="problems" class="py-20 bg-[#090D16] relative">
  <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
    <div class="text-center max-w-3xl mx-auto mb-16">
      <span class="text-xs font-mono font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-sky-400">
        The Reality of Legacy Systems
      </span>
      <h2 class="mt-3 text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-extrabold text-white tracking-tight">
        Is technical debt stalling your product velocity?
      </h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-base sm:text-lg text-slate-300">
        Legacy PHP codebases power massive revenues, but years of quick fixes and outdated versions eventually compound into high friction and dangerous risk.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6 lg:gap-8">
      {problems.map((problem) => (
        <div class="p-6 sm:p-8 rounded-2xl bg-slate-900/40 border border-slate-800/80 hover:border-slate-700 transition-all space-y-4">
          <div class="text-3xl">{problem.icon}</div>
          <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-white tracking-tight">{problem.title}</h3>
          <p class="text-slate-400 text-sm sm:text-base leading-relaxed">{problem.description}</p>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>

    <!-- The Solution Pivot -->
    <div class="mt-12 p-6 sm:p-8 rounded-2xl bg-gradient-to-r from-sky-950/40 via-slate-900 to-indigo-950/40 border border-sky-900/40 text-center sm:text-left sm:flex sm:items-center sm:justify-between gap-6">
      <div>
        <h4 class="text-lg font-bold text-white">There is a better way: Pragmatic Modernization</h4>
        <p class="text-sm text-slate-300 mt-1 max-w-2xl">
          You don't need a risky, multi-year rewrite. We modernize your existing PHP application incrementally in place while keeping production running smoothly.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="mt-4 sm:mt-0 shrink-0">
        <a
          href="#approach"
          class="inline-flex items-center text-sm font-semibold text-sky-400 hover:text-sky-300 gap-1.5"
        >
          <span>See How My Approach Works</span>
          <svg class="w-4 h-4" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor">
            <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M9 5l7 7-7 7" />
          </svg>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
